9;` so the decomposition is visible.\u0026#xA;4. Write `.ddx/executions/20260506T233300-cacee8d1/no_changes_rationale.txt` listing each child ID and slice, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A clean decomposition is a successful attempt. Do not mix partial implementation with decomposition.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC against concrete evidence (test name, file path, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `.ddx/executions/20260506T233300-cacee8d1/no_changes_rationale.txt` (what is done, what blocks, what a follow-up needs) before exiting. No commit and no rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`. A well-justified no_changes beats a bad commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If you write `.ddx/executions/20260506T233300-cacee8d1/no_changes_rationale.txt`, it MUST carry one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;one-line shell command\u0026gt;` — the loop runs it (cwd = project root, 60s); exit 0 closes the bead, non-zero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: needs_investigation` + `reason: \u0026lt;why\u0026gt;` — bead stays open for triage.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Bare rationales (\u0026#34;nothing to do\u0026#34;) are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Freestanding artifacts (investigation reports, findings docs) go under `.ddx/executions/20260506T233300-cacee8d1/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260506T233300-cacee8d1/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Bead overrides project defaults\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The bead description and AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and conservative project defaults (YAGNI, DOWITYTD, no-docs-unless-asked) in this worktree — write whatever the bead asks for.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-03f1e51b\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eExpose fiz run --harness as a hard pin\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nThe TerminalBench fiz-wrapper comparison profiles need to select Claude Code, Codex, or OpenRouter through fiz without duplicating adapter-specific flags in Harbor. The `fiz run` command currently exposes provider/model/model-ref options but not a harness hard pin, while routing docs already describe harness hard pins.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files:\u0026#xA;- agentcli run command flag definitions and option plumbing\u0026#xA;- cmd/fiz integration surface if needed\u0026#xA;- CLI help and option tests\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Out-of-scope:\u0026#xA;- service-layer routing semantics; depend on the service harness-pin bead\u0026#xA;- benchmark scripts and Harbor adapter changes\u0026#xA;- changing existing provider/model flag names\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Implementation notes:\u0026#xA;- Add `--harness \u0026lt;name\u0026gt;` to `fiz run`.\u0026#xA;- The flag must set the service-level harness pin, not just an environment variable.\u0026#xA;- Keep backward compatibility for existing provider/model/model-ref invocations.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. `fiz run --help` includes `--harness` and describes it as a harness hard pin.\u0026#xA;2. A CLI test proves `--harness codex` is passed into the service request/options used by `fiz run`.\u0026#xA;3. Existing CLI tests for provider/model/model-ref still pass.\u0026#xA;4. `go test ./agentcli ./cmd/fiz` passes.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:cli, area:harness, kind:task, phase:build\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-ed924ab3\" spec-id=\"terminalbench-fiz-wrapper-comparison-2026-05-06\" base-rev=\"11e077f62d2d743982aa74b16733cebf3103eb83\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260506T233300-cacee8d1\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"terminalbench-fiz-wrapper-comparison-2026-05-06\" path=\"docs/helix/02-design/terminalbench-fiz-wrapper-comparison-2026-05-06.md\"\u003eTerminalBench Fiz-Wrapper Comparison\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"attempt_id":"20260506T233300-cacee8d1","base_rev":"11e077f62d2d743982aa74b16733cebf3103eb83","bead_id":"fizeau-03f1e51b","bundle_path":